│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ heilbronn_local_refinement                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The previous attempt's returned configuration was not refined enough to be competitive.   │
│                          │ Instead of discarding whatever construction precedes it, this edit intercepts the final   │
│                          │ `return points` and applies a strong, fully deterministic local-optimization stage before │
│                          │ returning.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. **Scale-invariant objective**: The score is (min triangle area)/(convex hull area),    │
│                          │ which is invariant under affine scaling. So we can optimize all 13 points freely — the    │
│                          │ convex hull of the resulting points *is* the unit-area region after normalization.        │
│                          │ 2. **Vectorized evaluation**: All 286 triangle areas are computed with a single           │
│                          │ vectorized cross-product call, and hull area via a monotone-chain convex hull + shoelace  │
│                          │ formula, so thousands of objective evaluations fit comfortably in the time budget.        │
│                          │ 3. **Deterministic hill-climbing with restarts**: A fixed-seed RNG drives single-point    │
│                          │ perturbation moves with geometrically decaying step sizes. Random uniform restarts and    │
│                          │ jittered restarts around the incumbent best guard against poor local optima. Only         │
│                          │ improving moves are accepted, guaranteeing monotone progress and full reproducibility     │
│                          │ (seed 42).                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. **Numerical safety**: Duplicated points and degenerate hulls are guarded against, so   │
│                          │ the refinement degrades gracefully rather than crashing.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This turns any baseline configuration (lattice, random, or heuristic) into a locally      │
│                          │ optimized Heilbronn arrangement, maximizing the minimum normalized triangle area among    │
│                          │ all 286 triples.                                                                          │
