│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deterministic_heilbronn_solver                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The previous SEARCH block did not match the actual file contents. Based on the reported   │
│                          │ editable region, the file ends with a simple random point generator inside a function.    │
│                          │ This edit replaces the random-uniform generation with a full deterministic Heilbronn n=13 │
│                          │ optimizer, keeping the same function signature and return type (an (n, 2) NumPy array of  │
│                          │ points whose convex hull is normalized to unit area).                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Optimizes points freely in the plane (scale-invariant objective) and rescales so the   │
│                          │ convex hull has exactly unit area — the hull itself is the unit-area convex region, so    │
│                          │ all points are guaranteed inside/on it.                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Uses multiple structured seeds (3-fold symmetric concentric triangle shells + center   │
│                          │ point, regular 13-gon, hexagonal core, plus fixed-seed jittered variants).                │
│                          │ 3. Refines each seed with a targeted stochastic hill-climb: perturbs one vertex of one of │
│                          │ the 5 smallest-area triangles, accepts only strict improvements of min-triangle-area /    │
│                          │ hull-area, with adaptive step size (coarse-to-fine).                                      │
│                          │ 4. Enforces determinism via fixed seeds (42 preserved for compatibility, plus fixed       │
│                          │ internal seeds) and a wall-clock deadline for efficiency.                                 │
│                          │ 5. Includes a guarded symmetric fallback configuration and validation (13 finite, unique  │
│                          │ points) for robustness.                                                                   │
