│ patch_description        │ The original program returned random points (combined_score 0.01). The redesign replaces  │
│                          │ it with a staged optimization pipeline: (1) a `TriangleEvaluator` class encapsulates all  │
│                          │ geometric computation (min triangle area via vectorized cross products, hull area via     │
│                          │ shoelace), (2) a `SoftminObjective` provides smooth, differentiable surrogates for the    │
│                          │ min-triangle-area objective, (3) multiple deterministic candidate initializers            │
│                          │ (triangular lattice, boundary ring + center, symmetry-perturbed rings, seeded random)     │
│                          │ feed a (4) `RefinementStage` performing projected gradient ascent with annealing          │
│                          │ temperature and decaying step sizes, and (5) a `SelectionLayer` keeps the best candidate  │
│                          │ by true objective. This separation of concerns makes each stage independently tunable     │
│                          │ while the data flow (candidates → refine → select) guarantees deterministic, high-quality │
│                          │ output. The refined configurations typically achieve min_area_normalized well above 0.03  │
