│                          │ insight: since the convex region is defined as the convex hull of the points themselves,  │
│                          │ every configuration is feasible — the objective is simply (smallest of 286 triangle       │
│                          │ areas)/(hull area). We start from symmetric seeds (rings plus boundary points) and run    │
│                          │ coordinate perturbation hill climbing with a shrinking step size, recomputing the minimum │
│                          │ triangle area vectorized over all C(13,3)=286 triples (cheap: precomputed index array).   │
│                          │ Convex hull area is computed with a monotone chain hull. Fixed seed ensures determinism;  │
│                          │ the whole optimization completes in about a second, vastly improving min_area_normalized  │
│                          │ (from ~0.00 to above the benchmark, targeting combined_score > 1).                        │
