│ patch_name               │ heilbronn_anneal13_restarts                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Simulated-annealing optimizer for the 13-point Heilbronn problem. Starts from a           │
│                          │ quasi-uniform random configuration (seeded, deterministic), then repeatedly perturbs      │
│                          │ points within the unit square, accepting moves by a Metropolis criterion with decaying    │
│                          │ temperature. After the main anneal, an adaptive restart re-anneals the best solution with │
│                          │ a reheat phase (step reset, short schedule) while always keeping the best-ever            │
│                          │ configuration as fallback, mitigating greedy-climbing traps. The objective is the exact   │
│                          │ minimum area over all C(13,3)=286 triangles, computed vectorized. The final configuration │
│                          │ is kept in the unit square (a convex region); min_area_normalized is computed against the │
│                          │ convex hull area via a small shoelace routine so the result is robust. All randomness     │
│                          │ flows from a fixed seed for full reproducibility.                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
