│ patch_description        │ The current program recomputes all 286 triangle areas on every annealing step (wasting    │
│                          │ most of its 2500-iteration budget on redundant computation) and initializes from a single │
│                          │ perturbed grid. The new version: (1) maintains a cache of all triangle areas and          │
│                          │ incrementally updates only the 66 triples containing the moved point (with a partial-min  │
│                          │ trick), making each step ~5x cheaper so we can afford ~30k iterations across 6            │
│                          │ independent restarts; (2) uses boundary-heavy structured initializations (points on an    │
│                          │ ellipse plus interior center, and a 3-fold symmetric triangular layout) known to be       │
│                          │ favorable for Heilbronn-type problems, instead of only one grid seed; (3) uses an         │
│                          │ adaptive step/temperature schedule with greedy final polish; (4) keeps deterministic      │
│                          │ seeding (seed=42) and rescales the final configuration so the convex hull has unit area.  │
│                          │ More search, smarter starts, and incremental evaluation directly target the primary       │
│                          │ metric (min_area_normalized) while staying within time constraints.                       │
