│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ worst_triangle_annealing                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of the previous blind coordinate-descent polish over all points, this approach    │
│                          │ uses a fundamentally different paradigm: **worst-triangle targeted simulated annealing**. │
│                          │ At each step we compute all 286 triangle areas vectorized, identify the bottom-k smallest │
│                          │ ("bottleneck") triangles, and only perturb vertices involved in those bottlenecks. This   │
│                          │ concentrates search effort exactly where the objective is determined, avoiding wasted     │
│                          │ moves on already-good regions. Metropolis acceptance with a decaying temperature escapes  │
│                          │ local traps (addressing the greedy-climber problem), and a multi-start over several       │
│                          │ structured seeds (3-fold symmetric, hexagonal rings, jittered lattices) with a best-ever  │
│                          │ fallback guarantees robustness and determinism (fixed seeds). Points are kept inside the  │
│                          │ unit square; the objective is min-area / hull-area, so moves that shrink the hull are     │
│                          │ penalized automatically. Multi-scale reheats after the main anneal further refine.        │
