│ patch_description        │ Instead of stochastic simulated annealing, this approach uses **smooth-surrogate          │
│                          │ continuation with deterministic compass (pattern) search**. The non-smooth objective      │
│                          │ min(area) is replaced by a soft-min via LogSumExp with temperature T; we run a            │
│                          │ temperature homotopy (T: 0.05 → 0.002), optimizing the smooth surrogate at each stage     │
│                          │ with a deterministic coordinate-wise pattern search (try ±step per coordinate, accept     │
│                          │ improvements, shrink step on failure). The smooth surrogate gives usable descent          │
│                          │ directions even when the true minimum is tied among many triangles (a classic trap for    │
│                          │ greedy annealing), while the temperature schedule gradually sharpens the surrogate toward │
│                          │ the true objective. Multiple structured, deterministic initializations (rings, 3-fold     │
│                          │ symmetric triangle layout, grids) are all refined this way, followed by a strict greedy   │
│                          │ polish on the exact minimum, and the best configuration is rescaled to unit hull area.    │
│                          │ This is fully deterministic, gradient-free, and avoids the greedy-climbing trap that      │
│                          │ limits pure annealing.                                                                    │
