│ patch_description        │ The prior best program (score 0.67) used a soft objective (mean of the k smallest         │
│                          │ triangle areas) in the polish phase, which escapes flat minima where the true minimum     │
│                          │ cannot be improved by single coordinate moves. The current program regressed to a         │
│                          │ hard-min polish (0.58). This edit restores the soft-score polish, and additionally        │
│                          │ augments the annealing inner loop with an axis-wise directional fallback: when a Gaussian │
│                          │ 2-D move is rejected, try the four axis-aligned perturbations (±x, ±y) before rejecting — │
│                          │ as recommended. This exploits cheap vectorized rescoring and broadens the search within   │
│                          │ the time budget. To keep runtime in the ~4s sweet spot, annealing iterations are trimmed  │
│                          │ slightly (2000 + 600 reheat).                                                             │
