│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ normalized_objective_optimization                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The key flaw in the current optimizer is that the annealing/polish objectives use the     │
│                          │ **raw** minimum triangle area, not the normalized one (min_area / hull_area). During      │
│                          │ search, points can drift outward and grow the convex hull, inflating the raw minimum area │
│                          │ while the actual metric (normalized by hull area) stays flat or worsens — the optimizer   │
│                          │ climbs the wrong hill. Fix: make every accept/reject decision inside `_anneal` and        │
│                          │ `_polish` use the hull-normalized score. Additionally, add a repulsion-relaxed random     │
│                          │ initialization (points as mutually repelling particles) which is a classic good starting  │
│                          │ basin for Heilbronn-type problems, and slightly increase polish iterations for            │
│                          │ refinement. These changes are deterministic (fixed seed) and cost little extra time.      │
