│ patch_description        │ Implement the recommended "best-of-cycles" pool strategy: track the top-3 distinct        │
│                          │ configurations found across all seeds (diversity measured by mean pairwise point distance │
│                          │ > 0.1), then run one short reheat from each pool member plus one from the global best,    │
│                          │ followed by greedy polish on each. This escapes the plateau at min_area_normalized ~0.02  │
│                          │ by exploring multiple good basins instead of restarting only from single configs. Also    │
│                          │ add a few extra deterministic structured seeds (boundary-heavy and 13-gon) to broaden the │
│                          │ initial basin search, and slightly increase anneal iterations within time budget.         │
