│ patch_description        │ Add coordinate-axis fallback moves when the Gaussian targeted move is rejected in         │
│                          │ `_anneal`, and richer axis-search candidates in `_polish`. The full rescoring via         │
│                          │ `_score` is already cheap, so trying ±x/±y variants of the same rejected step costs       │
│                          │ almost nothing but gives directional diversity that isotropic Gaussian rejection lacks —  │
│                          │ worst triangles in Heilbronn configurations are often collinear triples that need a       │
│                          │ perpendicular (axis-aligned) correction. Also include a perpendicular nudge variant (both │
│                          │ axes) for near-collinear triples.                                                         │
