│                          │ Gaussian jitter, and a two-stage anneal+reheat pipeline. The current program regressed    │
│                          │ (0.67) by replacing push moves with axis-aligned jitter. I propose: (1) reintroduce       │
│                          │ push-move proposals in both the annealer and a new strict polish, (2) add a two-tier      │
│                          │ polish (K=8 then K=4, 2500 iters each) per the recommendation so late-stage refinement    │
│                          │ focuses on truly smallest triangles, (3) add reheat cycles from the global best with      │
