│                          │ retry uses only minimal, highly-likely anchor lines (`import numpy as np` and the final   │
│                          │ `return points`) to make the edit robust. The changes implement the recommended           │
│                          │ improvements: (1) precompute the sorted triangle-index triplet array once at module level │
│                          │ so it is shared across all seeds and iterations, (2) clamp perturbed candidate points to  │
│                          │ the unit box so moves that would leave the domain are repaired instead of                 │
│                          │ wasted/rejected, and (3) exit-early pruning — if a seed's best score after a modest       │
│                          │ number of iterations is far below the incumbent (less than 50%), abandon it and           │
│                          │ reallocate budget to more promising seeds, concentrating the iteration budget where it    │
│                          │ pays off. All changes are deterministic (no new randomness introduced).                   │
