│ patch_name               │ heilbronn13_tiered_pool_anneal                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the strongest elements of the two codebases: (1) the targeted     │
│                          │ worst-triangle annealing with geometric "push away from the small triangle's base line"   │
│                          │ moves, (2) the two-tier soft polish (K=8 then K=4 mean-of-smallest-areas greedy search)   │
│                          │ which empirically produced the best prior score (0.77), and (3) the current program's     │
│                          │ structured multi-start pool with crossover interpolation (interior-point mixing of good   │
│                          │ basins) plus the pentagon initializer for extra diversity. The pipeline: multi-start      │
│                          │ targeted anneal → two-tier polish per start → round-robin crossover reheat passes with    │
│                          │ pruning, always keeping the global best in the pool → final long two-tier polish on the   │
│                          │ champion. It retains the fast incremental area update idea (only recomputing areas,       │
│                          │ vectorized) and ends with a hull-area normalization to satisfy the unit-area convex       │
│                          │ region requirement, with deterministic seed 42. This should recover the ~0.77 score       │
│                          │ territory while the crossover passes add basin-mixing exploration without dominating      │
│                          │ runtime.                                                                                  │
