│ patch_name               │ softmin_gradient_continuation                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of stochastic Metropolis annealing, this uses analytic gradient ascent on a       │
│                          │ smooth soft-minimum surrogate: weights w_t = softmax(-alpha * area_t) over all 286        │
│                          │ triangles, with exact analytic gradients of the signed triangle areas (grad wrt vertex v  │
│                          │ = 0.5*w*sign*R(p_u - p_w)). A continuation schedule increases alpha over time so the      │
│                          │ surrogate tightens from "raise the average small triangles" to "raise the true minimum",  │
│                          │ sharpening the basin of attraction without random-walk noise. A per-restart adaptive step │
│                          │ controller (grow 1.05 on improvement, shrink 0.7 on regression) replaces fixed cooling    │
│                          │ ladders. Periodic rescaling to unit hull area makes the optimized quantity equal to the   │
│                          │ normalized score directly. Multi-start over structured inits, followed by a short         │
│                          │ targeted greedy polish on the K smallest triangles to squeeze the exact minimum. This     │
│                          │ should outperform annealing because every step follows the exact gradient direction of    │
│                          │ the binding constraint set rather than relying on random proposals, converging in fewer,  │
│                          │ better-directed iterations.                                                               │
