│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ heilbronn13_adaptive_axisanneal                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Combines Gen 29's adaptive acceptance-rate step controller with Gen 30's axis-fallback    │
│                          │ mechanism. Instead of a fixed geometric step decay, the annealer tracks acceptance rate   │
│                          │ over a sliding window of the last 200 proposals (counting both random-direction and       │
│                          │ axis-fallback acceptances). Below 15% acceptance the step halves; above 50% it multiplies │
│                          │ by 1.5 (capped at 0.05, floored at 0.002). Keeping the step in this "productive band"     │
│                          │ means the cheap coordinate-axis fallback directions fire more often, and the optimizer    │
│                          │ spends more iterations making real progress rather than rejecting oversized moves.        │
│                          │ Additional tweaks: pool deduplication tightened, and the polish stage uses adaptive step  │
│                          │ triads.                                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
